{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584310-off-with-the-fairies-and-back-again-\u2014-character-translation-thread","id":584310,"title":"Off With the Fairies and Back Again \u2014 Character Translation Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-08T23:37:21-07:00","id":584310,"title":"Off With the Fairies and Back Again \u2014 Character Translation Thread","content":"A couple years back my table made plans for a Changeling/Geist game that never got off the ground. Being the packrat nerds that we are, though, we held onto the characters for later use just the same. With the advent of the Second Editions and the emerging material for Changeling in particular, though, we recently discussed a bit of how the mechanical traits of the characters might need shifted and came up with some interesting stuff.<br /> <br /> For example, Sister Maggie Mulberry was a Darkling Antiquarian of the Autumn Court bent heavily toward the mystic-oneiromantic end of the fae demesne; a significant chunk of her Merits and Skills were invested in information-gathering tricks like Visionary Dreams and Hollow Archive. She had the bad luck to come out of Faerie twice as old as her fetch, so she took a bit of a blas\u00e9 attitude toward the prospect of reclaiming a mortal life, which she had been (and young Madge still was) somewhat detached from to begin with.<br /> <br /> Given that Maggie's choice of kith and seeming were sort of chosen to mechanically back her concept, 2e necessitates addressing those aspects in particular. The free Encyclopedic Knowledge that Antiquarians used to get no longer applies, and the bonuses to Academics and Investigation are likewise narrowed to being Informed in a particular area of focus that Maggie didn't really use all that much \u2014 she did her time in Faerie as a wrinkled thing at the bottom of a scrying pool, which didn't have much call to develop the kind of sense for history that the Antiquarians now emphasize. Similarly, her nature as a Darkling had been reverse-engineered into the more typical &quot;caught somewhere she wasn't supposed to be&quot; Durance-genesis that hooked into her Vice of Pride in a fashion that emphasized she was a curious sort; the 2e Darkling headspace doesn't quite fit into that narrative anymore.<br /> <br /> Overall, though, I'm fairly happy with the tentative result of recasting her as an Elemental Gray in 2e's mechanics until more options and information become available to more completely compare \u2014 &quot;perceptive recovering-egotist dreamrider&quot; fits nicely into the kith full of telepaths and the seeming full of post-hoc prophets in the meantime.<br /> <br /> By contrast, Milton the Wizened Drudge of the Winter Court, being built largely on the stealth-enhancements of kith and Court, turned out to require relatively little adjustment to fit into the Darkling archetype; his mien involved a lot of missing facial features and the character had a noted spiteful streak that tied into the 1e Wizened tendencies but just as easily transfers to 2e Darkling cynicism. Drudges weren't in the 2e kith sampler, but discussion suggests that the Chatelaines or their inheritors will probably pick up nicely for the character's lesser specialty of manipulating bureaucracies.<br /> <br /> Figured I'd make this thread in case anyone else wants to share similar ways their old characters end up filtering through the 2e paradigm shifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T15:47:41-07:00","id":586515,"title":"","content":"I've definitely been thinking a lot about how my existing 1e Changeling character would translate into 2e. Logor is, currently, a Waterborn Elemental of the Winter Court. Before his durance, he was a fairly successful high school athlete. He was involved in a variety of sports \u2013 track &amp; field, archery, soccer \u2013 but his favorite was always swimming. It was probably his skill in swimming that attracted his Keeper's attention. One summer, messing around with friends in a lake, he was dragged down into the depths of Arcadia. He was brought to the domain of a grand king of the ocean, where he was made into the king's personal messenger, little more than a sentient current of water that would carry missives of seaweed and coral throughout the kingdom. He remained in such a state, barely remembering who he was, until one day he saw a certain stone on his path. It was no more than a simple rock formation, but its shape was reminiscent of a blank human figure, with its arms outstretched. It stirred a memory, of his trophy case back home, of the things which had defined him before his whole had been taken from him. So instead of delivering his message, he followed the direction of the figure's arms, back through the Hedge, and back to his home. He regained some of his form, but not all of it; he came to resemble one of his trophies, with practically no identifying features aside from his toned athletic body.<br /> <br /> For 2e, he would definitely be some sort of aquatic Kith, but the only one that was revealed so far was the Nix. While the water-breathing fits there, the whole siren aspect doesn't mesh with his character. (I've really played up the whole &quot;elementals aren't good at emotions&quot; thing while playing him.) So I'd need to read the actual book with the full Kith list before I could make a decision, and if nothing there fits either, tweak something else or make my own Kith. <br /> Seeming-wise, however, he seems like a clear Wizened with the new paradigm. His &quot;craft&quot; is his athletics, being the fastest and most agile one on the field or in the water. His Durance story would need to be tweaked, especially his escape, but it could pretty easily be interpreted as using his mastery of the craft to escape. But in particular, the idea of having to rebuild himself fits in perfectly with the Wizened paradigm, even if I have to swap some order of events around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}